From: RelayLM cache diagnostic
Subject: [DIAGNOSTIC ONLY] preserve and dump Gemma4 layer-0 pre/post projection rows

Target: ggml-org/llama.cpp @ e2d2c0d6aa9b996d5d3a3c1d5e24c8c19728bb3d
Prerequisite patch:
  e2d2c0d6-gemma4-kv-logical-prefix-dump-diagnostic.patch

This patch is diagnostic instrumentation only. It does not insert arithmetic
nodes and deliberately does not use cb_eval, because the frozen scheduler's
eval callback changes graph execution grouping at observed nodes.

When LLAMA_PROJECTION_ORIGIN_PROBE_DIR and LLAMA_PROJECTION_ORIGIN_PROBE_LABEL
are set, the existing layer-0 attn_norm, Kcur, and Vcur tensors are marked as
graph outputs so their buffers survive until the full ubatch graph has
completed. The tensors are copied to host only after scheduler synchronization.

diff --git a/src/llama-context.cpp b/src/llama-context.cpp
--- a/src/llama-context.cpp
